        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T13:46:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, is this going to ripple out and force us to add in the vector of tracked recorders? (https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/600344)\n\nWhat about making this `SK_DEBUG` instead?",
      "parentUuid": "a447e75a_fc0f84fc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "a31578f016e11330e931da320f2735afa3771548",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f43aa69_13b46ca6",
        "filename": "include/gpu/graphite/Recorder.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T13:55:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, that\u0027s my concern, though I was thinking in that case of adding an allocated struct that wraps both the boolean and the vector, if it\u0027s needed (something like std::unique_ptr\u003cContextTestInfo\u003e). It can\u0027t be debug only, that would break readPixels in release.\n\nFor the ContextOptions I was thinking of adding an fTestInfo void* member, that defaults to nullptr but otherwise could be reinterpreted as a pointer to a struct that only the test code knows about.",
      "parentUuid": "d2a5412f_d820e780",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "a31578f016e11330e931da320f2735afa3771548",
